(text "R703 is within the40–200k selection range.\nR704 pulls up in the Ethernet domain only.\nR679 remains a47k local pulldown at U11.\nNo capacitor is placed on PERSTB." (at 17.78 220.98 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left top)) (uuid "51054686-beb5-531c-b50e-f87d5abba274"))
(rectangle (start 208.28 144.78) (end 406.4 248.92000000000002) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default) (color 60 110 145 1)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "6224a1b0-7043-5e98-9b90-6365ff855b46"))
(text "Shared condition bus and validation boundaries" (at 212.09 148.59 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d4184521-20b5-5974-985c-928940c6462f"))
(text "ETH_RESET_CONDITION_N joins U12 PG, U13 PG and U15 Y.\nR653/R663 pull up to Ethernet3.3V; any LOW holds reset.\nTP651/TP661 now observe this same shared condition.\nThe normal soft starts finish well before the180ms\nminimum delay expires. Configure stable REFCLK before\nraising host PERST; it must precede U11 release by100us.\n\nFast power-loss reset is NOT yet qualified: regulator PG\nhas40us typical deglitch with no guaranteed maximum.\nA fast fault path and its timing remain required work." (at 215.9 170.18 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left top)) (uuid "71401737-823f-5024-8aa3-95fd1a1f9a88"))
(text "RTL8125BG Table35: >=100ms stable power, >=100us assertion/clock lead, >=10ms between releases.\nTPS3808 delay closes the normal-startup timing; abrupt faults, repeated power cycles and the final boot image still require qualification." (at 15.24 269.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5f38902e-2996-5eaa-9058-6f5a2b74d4b4"))
)
